Proposed (30.3s): Use this skill whenever the user wants any prompt or LLM instruction text improved, fixed, reviewed, rewritten, or newly written — task prompts, system prompts, chatbot/support-bot instructions, agent scaffolding, RAG assistant instructions, SKILL.md and slash-command files. Trigger on intent, not wording: the user pastes or describes such a prompt and complains about its output (too long, off-script, misses things, worse after a model upgrade), asks to reword, trim, modernize, punch up, or "make better" the prompt, asks why it isn't working, or says "prompt engineer this" / "enhance this prompt" / /prompt-enhancer. A quoted prompt plus dissatisfaction with its results means use this skill, even if the text is called instructions, a command, or a persona. Do NOT use when the user wants the underlying task itself performed, or asks about LLM APIs, prompt-injection security, translation, or code that merely handles prompts. Includes /prompt-enhancer:run-evals for A/B testing.

